  "body": "P0 (#84): no drilling op checked the tool's reach - with a short flute the shank or holder fed into uncut stock unflagged; #77's raw-stock mouths made it far more likely (~16 mm deep vs ~6 mm).\n\n**What changed** (new `crates/app/src/operation/drill_reach.rs`; one call each in `cross_spindle.rs` and `generate.rs`)\n- **Reach**: every drilling cycle (axial and cross) refuses by name a hole deeper from the stock surface than the tool's `flute_len` - e.g. \"cross hole 0 at (10.000, 0.000, 0.000) is 16.000 mm deep from the stock surface; tool DR-0400's flute reaches 12.000 mm ...\". Cross holes: depth from the raw-surface mouths (#77) plus the through-hole exit allowance (spot cycles: the dimple depth). Axial holes: from the highest material over the drill's (or a wider shank's) footprint - the part, plus the setup stock capped at the R plane - down to the cycle bottom, read from the kernel's own cycle records. No exception for necked tools.\n- **Holder** (`holder_d` x `holder_len`, `flute_len + shank_len` behind the tip; none when `holder_d`/`holder_len` is 0): on axial holes its face must stay above the material over its footprint; on the cross drill, on every rapid and feed, its lower edge rides above the stock's Z top or its swept footprint stays outside the stock radius. The opposite-station end-face swing is refused, not raised (raising Clearance drills it).\n\n**Fixtures that now refuse - all real reach collisions**: `cross_support` (a 31 mm through hole, 47 mm from the raw box, on a 12 mm flute -> 50 mm flute), `drilling_cross_stock` (16-24 mm from the raw bar -> 30 mm flute), `blind_floor` / `solid_law` drill gouge tests (14-15 mm -> 30 mm), `operations::moving_the_part_marks_the_drill_op_stale_until_regen` (13 mm -> 20 mm). `operations::a_hole_deeper_than_the_drill_reaches_warns_and_still_generates` pinned the old design (generate + warn + post blocks) and is now `..._is_refused_by_name`; `posting::a_warned_path_blocks_even_though_it_generated` now uses a contour whose shank rubs the wall. The verifier's own reach warning stays as a backstop.\n\n**Pinned by** `drill_reach::{a_short_flute_cross_drill_on_raw_stock_wider_than_the_part_is_refused_by_name, a_holder_that_would_sweep_the_end_face_on_the_swing_is_refused_by_name, an_axial_hole_deeper_than_the_flute_from_the_stock_top_is_refused_by_name, the_same_cross_hole_drills_with_a_flute_long_enough}` (first three failed on main) + 2 unit tests.\n\n**Gates**: quick gate green (app 437 s, ui 42 s); the agent ran 20+ app binaries one by one, the app lib tests and 3 UI drilling tests; goldens unchanged; clippy -D warnings clean.\n\n**Known cost**: with stock declared, a hole on a pocket floor may be falsely refused (drilling doesn't know what earlier ops removed) - fails safe; #89.\n\nChangelog: fix(app): drilling refuses a hole deeper than the drill's flute from the stock surface, and proves the holder clear of the stock (incl. the cross-drill end-face swing)\n\nFixes #84\n",
